# Normalize line endings deterministically across OSes.
#
# Batch / cmd scripts MUST be CRLF: cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only .bat files
# (multi-line `if (...)` blocks blow up with ". was unexpected at this time"
# and REM lines get executed). Without this rule a Unix tool (sed, etc.) or a
# Linux CI checkout can silently ship an LF .bat that fails on Windows.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts MUST be LF: bash chokes on a trailing CR ("\r: command not found").
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Everything else: normalize to LF in the repo, let Git pick the working-tree EOL.
*       text=auto
